[0;35mReviewed and fixed several issues.

Key fixes made:
- Added selective cleanup of stale derived outputs in the task output directory, without touching raw inputs.
- Fixed representative-window selection for the “before Mw 7.1” figure so it only uses intervals between Mw 6.4 and Mw 7.1.
- Added explicit validation that the mainshock file contains exactly one Mw 6.4 and one Mw 7.1 event.
- Added downstream schema checks after preprocessing and after the interval-summary merge.
- Fixed a low-support edge case in pair counting for `n < 2`.
- Relaxed the direction-metric validity test so it rejects only all-NaN directional vectors, not any vector containing a NaN.
- Added one more final validation check for interval-summary row count consistency.
- Removed a few unused imports/constants to reduce correctness risk and review noise.

So this is not a pure “passed as-is” review; the script needed corrections and has now been updated accordingly.[0m

